From 4466fe50f6c72ef383ed88cbac370d5ef7e9f946 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 17:26:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Admin console: search/filter, friendlier errors, bulk
 cleanup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The admin list pages only offered an "Add new" form with no way to
search or filter, and any constraint violation (duplicate name, FK
still referenced) crashed to Next's generic error page instead of
saying what went wrong. Both made routine data cleanup painful and
error-prone.

- AdminTableFilter: client-side search + country filter bar, wired
  into every admin list page (hospital groups/sites, deployments,
  procurement notices, health authorities). Deployments also gains a
  derived Country column and inline delete (previously delete-only-
  via-detail-page).
- CollapsibleFormCard: the "Add new" form is now collapsed by default
  so it doesn't read as the page's main action.
- lib/dbErrors.ts + ErrorBanner: known Postgres constraint violations
  (unique, FK) are caught and redirected back as a readable banner
  instead of an opaque "Application error" / digest page.
- lib/db.ts: add transaction() — query() opens a fresh pooled
  connection per call, so a bare BEGIN/COMMIT across separate query()
  calls was never actually atomic.
- New bulk cleanup action + page (/admin/hospital-groups/bulk-cleanup):
  delete a batch of hospital groups by exact name, cascading through
  their sites and deployments in the correct FK order inside one
  transaction per group. Refuses to touch (and reports separately)
  any group/site still linked to a contact or procurement notice, so
  a name-cleanup pass can't silently destroy unrelated evidence.
